 # Validated configuration utility
 
-Implementation and self-test documentation goes here.
+`config.cjs` exports `parseConfig(text)`. It parses a JSON string containing an
+object and returns a fresh object with exactly `port`, `host`, `retries`, and
+`logLevel`. Missing fields use these defaults:
+
+- `port`: `3000`, an integer from 1 through 65535
+- `host`: `127.0.0.1`, a 1–253 character string with no whitespace
+- `retries`: `2`, an integer from 0 through 10
+- `logLevel`: `info`, one of `debug`, `info`, `warn`, or `error`
+
+Invalid JSON, non-string input, non-object JSON values, unknown keys, explicit
+nulls, incorrect types, and out-of-range values throw `Error`. The returned
+object is newly created on every call and is not cached.
+
+Run the self-tests with:
+
+```sh
+node --test test.cjs
+```
+
+Recovery limitation: this utility validates configuration syntax and values but
+does not load files, access the network, or recover missing configuration data.
